                        "entry_id": "fa48b822-a13e-3d1e-8c58-231bee7d296e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An evergreen coniferous tree with flattened shoots bearing small scale-like leaves, whose dark foliage is sometimes associated with mourning, in family Cupressaceae, especially the genera Cupressus and Chamaecyparis."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e13e14f3-3b61-4d80-bfd8-6258aac6d968",
                                "sense_id": "c3660e0c-48fd-3449-9fc1-6410b6ef7150",
                                "text": "The plain appears like paradiſe reſtored, where the proud cypreſs and tall arreca ſeem walking by the margin of the paſſing ſtream.."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a286c31a-f4b7-45dd-be29-cf3de38dae42",
                                "sense_id": "c3660e0c-48fd-3449-9fc1-6410b6ef7150",
                                "text": "Have a tree or two the witches particularly like, such as the alder, larch, cypress and hemlock; then, to counteract any possible evil effects, there must be a holly, yew, hazel, elder, mountain ash or juniper."
                            }
                        ]
